# Goose Hints for Nix Configuration

## Project Structure
This is a Nix flake-based dotfiles repository using:
- flake-parts for organization
- import-tree for automatic module discovery
- home-manager for user environment management

## Coding Standards
- Sort Nix flake properties alphabetically for consistency
- Use 2 space indentation
- Follow NixOS module patterns
- Keep modules small and focused
- Use descriptive variable names
- Prefer explicit over implicit configuration
- Do not use commas to separate items in Nix lists (Nix uses whitespace separation)

## Flake Input Management
- Pin all flake inputs with specific revisions when possible
- Use `follows` relationships to ensure compatible versions
- Keep inputs minimal and purpose-driven

## Module Organization
- Group related configurations into logical modules
- Use consistent naming conventions across modules
- Document module purposes in comments
- Separate generic configurations from host-specific ones